Subject: [PATCH] OvmfPkg/SioBusDxe: a PS/2 mouse child, so Ps2MouseDxe binds

SioBusDxe makes the ISA children of q35's LPC bridge from a fixed table:
COM1, COM2 and the PS/2 keyboard (PNP0303, UID 0). Ps2MouseDxe binds only
to PNP0F03, PNP0F13, or PNP0303 with UID 1, so on q35 it never binds and
QEMU's PS/2 mouse (the i8042's auxiliary port) has no
EFI_SIMPLE_POINTER_PROTOCOL.

Add a PNP0F03 (Microsoft PS/2-style mouse) child, UID 0, sharing the
keyboard controller's ports 0x60 and 0x64. It goes after the existing
entries, so their indices and device paths are unchanged. Ps2MouseDxe
then gives PciRoot(0x0)/Pci(0x1F,0x0)/Acpi(PNP0F03,0x0) a SimplePointer.
QEMU sends PS/2 mouse events only while no other mouse (USB, virtio) is
its active one.

axl-firmware's patch against edk2-stable202611, applied after
0005-pci-serial.patch to a copy of the packages it touches.

---
diff --git a/OvmfPkg/SioBusDxe/SioService.c b/OvmfPkg/SioBusDxe/SioService.c
index 66c5a08..c03bcee 100644
--- a/OvmfPkg/SioBusDxe/SioService.c
+++ b/OvmfPkg/SioBusDxe/SioService.c
@@ -73,7 +73,12 @@ SIO_DEVICE_INFO  mDevicesInfo[] = {
     EISA_PNP_ID (0x303),
     0,
     { (ACPI_SMALL_RESOURCE_HEADER *)&mPs2KeyboardDeviceResources }
-  }   // PS/2 Keyboard Controller
+  },  // PS/2 Keyboard Controller
+  {
+    EISA_PNP_ID (0xF03),
+    0,
+    { (ACPI_SMALL_RESOURCE_HEADER *)&mPs2KeyboardDeviceResources }
+  }   // PS/2 Mouse, on the keyboard controller's auxiliary port
 };
 
 //
